		<!-- Complete 6-Step DIY Photo Booth Master Guide -->
		<section class="hand-card" style="padding: 1.75rem; background: #fff; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
			<h2 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.45rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--fg-pencil); padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
				📚 Complete Step-by-Step Guide: How to Build a Portable DIY Wedding Photo Booth
			</h2>

			<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(310px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem;">
				
				<!-- Step 1: Software & Automation -->
				<div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
					<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
						<span style="background: var(--accent-red); color: #fff; font-weight: 900; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.85rem;">1</span>
						<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-weight: 700;">Software & 4-Screen Automation</h3>
					</div>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
						Choose dedicated photo booth software (e.g. <em>DSLR Remote Pro / Breeze</em> for Canon/Nikon, <em>DSLRBooth</em>, <em>Sparkbooth</em>, or <em>LumaBooth</em> for iPad). Configure the <strong>4 automated user screens</strong>: (1) Start Screen with branded wedding graphics, (2) 3-2-1 Countdown with live mirror view, (3) 1-second "Smile!" flash screen, and (4) Processing progress bar while the printer outputs strips.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Step 2: The Big Red Start Button -->
				<div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
					<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
						<span style="background: var(--accent-red); color: #fff; font-weight: 900; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.85rem;">2</span>
						<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-weight: 700;">The 4" Arcade Button Trigger</h3>
					</div>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
						Never leave a mouse or keyboard for guests. Mount a <strong>4-inch illuminated red arcade dome push button</strong> on the interior shelf. Connect the microswitch to a zero-delay USB arcade encoder board (or hacked USB serial adapter) mapped to the spacebar. Power the internal 12V LED so the button glows enticingly inside the booth!
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Step 3: PVC Frame Construction -->
				<div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
					<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
						<span style="background: var(--accent-red); color: #fff; font-weight: 900; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.85rem;">3</span>
						<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-weight: 700;">Portable PVC Frame Cut Sheet</h3>
					</div>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
						Build a <strong>6 ft high × 40 inch wide × 48 inch deep</strong> frame using 3/4" furniture-grade PVC pipe: (10) 3/4" pipes, (10) 3-way corner elbows, (12) 4-way cross connectors, and (10) T-joints. Build an 18" deep electronics tower with two support legs to hold the monitor and camera shelf. Spray-paint exposed pipes satin black.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Step 4: Fabric Curtains & 11x17 Bezel -->
				<div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
					<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
						<span style="background: var(--accent-red); color: #fff; font-weight: 900; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.85rem;">4</span>
						<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-weight: 700;">Fabric Panels & Monitor Bezel</h3>
					</div>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
						Cut 6 ft fabric panels hemmed with heat-bonded fabric tape or sewn hems, attached to PVC rails with heavy-duty Velcro strips. Cut a rectangular window in the front panel for the monitor and camera, and frame the cut fabric edges with an <strong>11×17 inch wooden picture frame</strong> held with thumb tacks for a clean, pro look.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Step 5: Camera Settings & Power -->
				<div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
					<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
						<span style="background: var(--accent-red); color: #fff; font-weight: 900; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.85rem;">5</span>
						<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-weight: 700;">Camera Settings & Continuous Power</h3>
					</div>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
						Set your camera to <strong>Manual (M) mode: Shutter 1/125s, Aperture f/6.3 or f/8</strong> (ensures sharp focus for multiple faces across different depths), and ISO 400-800. Power the camera via an <strong>AC dummy battery coupler</strong> plugged into a surge protector so you never have to change batteries.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Step 6: Guestbook Scrapbook Station -->
				<div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
					<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
						<span style="background: var(--accent-red); color: #fff; font-weight: 900; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.85rem;">6</span>
						<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-weight: 700;">Scrapbook Protocol & Perforated Strips</h3>
					</div>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
						Configure the printer for duplicate 2x6" strips on 4x6" paper. Provide <strong>pre-perforated paper</strong> so guests easily snap prints in half. Supply <strong>double-sided tape runners</strong> and <strong>metallic gel pens</strong> that dry in 3 seconds without smudging when the guestbook album is closed.
					</p>
				</div>

