		<section class="hand-card" style="padding: 1.75rem; background: #fff; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
			<h2 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 1.25rem;">
				❓ Frequently Asked Questions: Building a Wedding Photo Booth
			</h2>
			
			<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;">
				<div style="border-bottom: 1px dashed #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 0.85rem;">
					<h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 0.35rem;">
						Where can I buy the 3-way and 4-way PVC corner joints?
					</h3>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;">
						Standard hardware stores (like Home Depot or Lowe's) usually only stock basic plumbing T-joints and 90-degree elbows. For structural corner joints, purchase furniture-grade 3/4" 3-way and 4-way PVC fittings online from specialty suppliers like <em>Formufit</em> or Amazon.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div style="border-bottom: 1px dashed #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 0.85rem;">
					<h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 0.35rem;">
						How do you wire the arcade start button to a laptop?
					</h3>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;">
						The simplest method is using a <strong>Zero-Delay USB Arcade Encoder Board</strong> ($10 on Amazon). Connect the two microswitch terminals on the button to the encoder's "Button 1" input, and plug the USB cable into your laptop. Set your photo booth software to trigger on that button or mapped spacebar key.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div>
					<h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 0 0 0.35rem;">
						How fast does the printer need to be to prevent reception lines?
					</h3>
					<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;">
						Compact dye-sub photo printers like the Canon Selphy take ~40 seconds to output a 4x6" print, which is great for weddings up to 130 guests. For larger weddings (150-250+ guests), rent or buy a commercial high-speed dye-sub printer (like the DNP DS-RX1HS) that spits out dry, glossy strips in just 12 seconds.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
